<!--
  Pioneer DJ DDJ-FLX4: a Cadence profile from the online library (A208).

  SOURCE, and only this: the manufacturer's own MIDI documentation.
    DDJ-FLX4 List of MIDI messages (Ver 1.0) (AlphaTheta Corporation (Pioneer DJ), 2022-10-20 (PDF date; © 2022)), pages 1-5
    https://downloads.support.alphatheta.com/software_info/dj-controllers/DDJ-FLX4/DDJ-FLX4_MIDI_message_List_E1.pdf
    DDJ-FLX4 - MIDI-compatible software (links the list above) (AlphaTheta Help Center, accessed 2026-11-07), pages n/a
    https://support.alphatheta.com/en-US/articles/12294087060377
    DDJ-FLX4 Instruction Manual (DRI1804A) (AlphaTheta Corporation (Pioneer DJ), 2022-10-24 (PDF date; © 2022)), pages 16 (CUE/LOOP CALL halves/doubles), 60 (Beat Jump pads), 64 (Beat Loop pads), 144-146 (Utilities mode), 151 (MIDI device name), 161 (other DJ applications)
    https://downloads.support.alphatheta.com/manuals/dj-controllers/DDJ-FLX4/DDJ-FLX4_DRI1804A_manual.pdf
  No mapping file from any other application was read or used.

  status="manual": the message is the manufacturer's. Nobody has tried this map on the hardware
  yet. If a control does nothing, use Learn on that row and tell us at shlabs.contact@gmail.com.
  label="..." is the control's name on the unit, shown in the mapping dialog and the guided tour.

  BEFORE YOU START: None documented. The unit sends these messages over USB as soon as it is connected; the manual lists no MIDI-mode setting in Utilities mode. Vinyl mode is ON by default, so the jog top sends CC 34. AlphaTheta's help page says to power the unit off and on again after you switch from one DJ application to another.

  CADENCE'S CHOICES:
    the jog is the platter TOP's turn with Vinyl mode on (CC 34), the unit's default. With Vinyl mode off the top sends CC 35, and the wheel's side sends its own message: Learn either to the jog row if that is how you play.
    Not bound, because one target holds one control: Deck 1 CUE button (ch1.cuepad1), since Deck 1 performance pad 1, HOT CUE mode takes ch1.cuepad1; Deck 2 CUE button (ch2.cuepad1), since Deck 2 performance pad 1, HOT CUE mode takes ch2.cuepad1.

  LEFT OUT (no Cadence target): SHIFT button (note 63) and all +SHIFT messages; Jog touch (note 54), jog outer wheel turn (CC 33), jog turn with Vinyl mode off (CC 35), SHIFT+jog (CC 41): only one jog message can feed chN.jog; IN (note 16) and OUT (note 17) loop buttons: no loop-in/loop-out target; BEAT SYNC long press (note 92); TEMPO slider (CC 0/32): no tempo target; TRIM knobs (CC 4/36): no trim target (chN.gain is the channel fader); Beat FX section: FX CH SELECT, FX SELECT, BEAT ◁/▷, LEVEL/DEPTH, FX ON/OFF; MASTER CUE button (ch 7 note 99): master.cue is the headphone mix knob, not this button; Crossfader (ch 7 CC 31/63), MIC LEVEL, SMART CFX, SMART FADER, Android MONO/STEREO switch; Pad mode buttons (HOT CUE 27, PAD FX1 30, BEAT JUMP 32, SAMPLER 34 on ch 1/2) and pads 5-8 in BEAT LOOP mode, pads 3-8 in BEAT JUMP mode, PAD FX / SAMPLER / KEYBOARD / KEY SHIFT pad pages; Fader start / crossfader start notes (102, 82), channel level meter and LOADED/VINYL MODE MIDI-OUT messages

  A jog wheel that moves too fast or too slow: set its row to Fine, or invert it, in the dialog.
-->
